module tail_if_let_value.neg_1

// A TAIL `if let` USED AS A VALUE WITH NO `else` -- still refused, and this
// cell is why the fix is a fix rather than a hole.
//
// The None path produces nothing, so the function would fall off its end. That
// is not a subset limit but a fact about the shape, and the plain tail `if` is
// refused in the same words for the same reason (274.7 B14).
//
// WHAT IT GUARDS is the CONDITION on the allow-list, not the message. Letting
// `IfLet` into the list of value tails unconditionally is the easy version of
// the 1189 fix and it would compile this file into a function with no return
// value. The pair to this cell is `pos_1.nv`: one form accepted, its
// else-less twin refused, and neither can be green without the other being
// looked at.

// NOVAC_EXPECT ends without a value

fn g(o Option[int]) -> int {
    if Some(v) = o { v }
}
